            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This commit is unreviewable.  You've got a design in mind so you put together some infrastructure that isn't even being used.  Please merge this at least into one commit that uses the infrastructure.\n\nAs written, I have no idea why we are creating a virtual class and prefer we do not."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "I agree that the commit in its current form doesn\u2019t tells the usage of the infrastructure.\n\nDiscoveryProtocol (Abstract Class)\n\n  discoverDevices(): std::vector<ResponderInfo> = 0\n\n  getType(): TransportType = 0\n\nConcrete Implementations\n\n   MCTPDiscoveryProtocol\n\n   TCPDiscoveryProtocol\n\n   PCIEDiscoveryProtocol\n  (All inherit from DiscoveryProtocol)\n\nSPDMDiscovery (Context)\n\n   SPDMDiscovery(std::unique_ptr<DiscoveryProtocol>)\n\n   discover(): bool\n\n\nBy following this design, adding a new transport simply requires creating a new class that inherits from DiscoveryProtocol. No changes are needed in the SPDMDiscovery class.\n\nlet me know your thoughts on this"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "I am implementing the Strategy Design Pattern to make the transport layer easily extensible."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "At what point do you intend to have unit tests?  There isn't a single unit test in this entire stack."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "We will add it in the later commits, We have it in the downstream but I am just breaking and making the modification to align with the merged design and start using the libspdm, We have our own libspdmd but we are migrating to start using the dmtf libspdm."
                }
            ],
